2324 0 obj
<<
/Title (Initial findings highlighted a key constraint: Optimum Lap initially assumed maximum motor torque was available continuously, irrespective of the vehicle's instantaneous operating conditions. As a result, the  model predicted significantly higher energy consumption, indicating that an \(unrealistically\) large accumulator would be required to complete the endurance event. This behaviour was identified as an inherent limitation of the Optimum Lap model, which does not account for throttle variation and therefore overestimates energy demand.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2320 0 R
/Next 2328 0 R
>>
